ious\" and \"uncooperative\". That suggests issues with crew cooperation and professional communication. Also we have no explicit note about attention to numeric information, but we have \"excellent computer skills\" which may imply good handling of numeric data, but we shouldn't infer beyond explicit. However we can note that we have no direct evidence about numeric attention.\n\nWe need to state our current recommendation. Our current vote is Candidate C (as per earlier). We need to either maintain or change based on new evidence. We can argue that B's cooperation and communication concerns are significant, making C still the best despite feedback issue. Or we could shift if we think B's strengths outweigh C's concerns. But we have to be consistent with our vote in metadata. We can keep vote Candidate C, explaining why.\n\nThus: Public message: I agree with Agent 2 that we need more detail, but based on the facts we have, B shows uncooperative behavior and sometimes wrong tone, indicating crew cooperation and professional communication concerns. This weakens B relative to C, whose leadership and situational awareness are strong, and while C has feedback issues, they are manageable with training. Therefore I still recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: B can be uncooperative, sometimes adopts wrong tone, pretentious; C anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, leadership. Also note that we have no evidence about B's numeric attention.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
